A||||10||gusto||short shifter for auto trans.??||||5||
Z||000000||gusto||12-19-2001||04:04 PM||||Is there such a thing? I've only heard of them being in manuals. If not could it be manufactured? I know I'm not the first to think of this. Would there be any kind of problems with it?     -Thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||12-19-2001||04:13 PM||||Short Auto Shifter??  Any reason inparticular?  I believe that Rodney Dickman has an adaptor to make your auto shifter look like a manual (chrome shaft, ball shifter).  You press down on the ball instead of pusing the side button.  Is that more of what you're looking for?<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||gusto||12-19-2001||04:36 PM||||Yeah, thats pretty much it. But I want it more to clear space around the radio, not to look like a manual. Any info you could give me would be greatly appreciated.                       -Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000003||seadog||12-19-2001||05:29 PM||||Gusto,  I Have an automatic with the shifter shortened, The bottom of the Knobs neck is only slightly higher than the PRND21 surface. It was done by the previous owner of the car so I am going by what I THINK I see. You might remove your shift knob (pull out the staple retainer on the front of the base and twist up) and note the height of the white plastic bead thingy above the end of the shaft *this is the link that depresses when you press the button to shift. I would think you could cut the hollow shaft to the height you want, Don't forget to allow for what goes into the knob.  Then cut the plastic link to the same length out the shaft as before and re- install the knob.<BR> A couple of things to know, you lose locking the knob with the staple, however one or two<BR>wraps of 3/4" masking tape works fine on mine.<BR> Also the stock shift boot is not very pliable and in my case broke a plastic catch for the elastic band. I am going to glue it back and get a better auto shift boot from Rodney.<BR> any one else?                                              Cheers, Richard <P>  <P> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||12-19-2001||05:56 PM||||My auto shifter has been shortened by Bam Bam. He has done mine and a few others. Very nice quality and you can use any GM auto shift knob including the stick one! You still use the "staple" to hold the knob on.<BR>As for the boot, Mine has no problems. I am using a "cobra head" handle from a Bonneville SSEi. <BR>Here's the thread for those interested.<BR>There are before and after pics in the thread too!<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/002204.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/002204.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">             <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT><P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-19-2001).]||||reg||14
